You have not adequately understood the melee system. The twoweaponing
to-hit and damage modifiers are not *added* to your existing skill-based
to-hit and damage modifiers; they replace them outright. Your proposal
did not suggest changing this.

>Now that the intel FP bugs are fixed, why not take advantage of
>floating point math by replacing a lot of formulas in the form of:
[formula easy to comprehend and predict, albeit with some significant
flaws]
>with stuff more like:
[formula rather less easy to comprehend and predict, and possessed of
its own set of weaknesses]
>So a 30 attacking a 10 (adjusting for all of this AD&D AC10 nonsense)
>would be a 75% chance of success rather than 100%.

Come up with a way to fix the ludicrous hypereffectiveness of damage
spells first, then we can think about proposals to completely rewrite
the melee to-hit system.

(Simplest solution: Make magic missile stop at the first creature it
scores an unreflected hit on.)
